WEBVTT

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:05.167
An operations agent can answer questions

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.167
and call tools.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.100
But who owns it, what can it access,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.667
and how do you trace its actions?

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.067
Microsoft Agent 365 is the control plane

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.567
for observing, governing, and securing agents.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.267
It is not the agent builder or runtime.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.833
Observe: bring inventory and activity into view,

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:27.400
then trace agent invocations and tool calls.

00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:31.400
Govern: establish ownership, identities,

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.400
permissions, and lifecycle controls.

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:37.733
Secure: connect identity, data protection,

00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:39.300
and threat detection through Entra,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.533
Purview, and Defender.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.600
When code-level integration is needed,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.400
add only the SDK capabilities required.

00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:49.967
Keep your existing framework and hosting.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.800
Start with one accountable pilot.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.567
Verify licensing and preview limitations,

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:59.300
test the controls, then expand with evidence.
